  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Trying to ingest an object into Fedora fails if the document contains a reference to an external resource and the Fedora server is only allowed to access that resource via a HTTP proxy.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "My first idea to solve this was to set the environment variable CATALINA_OPTS to something like",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "CATALINA_OPTS=\"-Dhttp.proxyHost=proxy.fiz-karlsruhe.de -Dhttp.proxyPort=8888\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "and restart Tomcat.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Unfortunately this isn't sufficient because the HTTPClient module which Fedora uses doesn't read that properties automatically.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So the next step was to set the proxy parameters into the HTTPClient in WebClient.java just after a new instance of the HTTPClient was created (see attached file).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "That's all. Maybe someone else has the same problem.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Best regards,",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "AndrÃ©",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
